## 📁 Project Structure Rules

### Clean Architecture Layers (Per Service)

```text
MyApp.[Service]/
├── MyApp.[Service].API/              # Presentation Layer
│   ├── Controllers/                  # HTTP endpoints, routing
│   ├── Program.cs                    # DI, middleware, configuration
│   └── appsettings.*.json            # Environment configurations
│
├── MyApp.[Service].Application/      # Application Layer
│   ├── Services/                     # Business logic orchestration
│   ├── Contracts/                    # Service interfaces, DTOs
│   └── Mappings/                     # AutoMapper profiles
│
├── MyApp.[Service].Domain/           # Domain Layer (Pure)
│   ├── Entities/                     # Domain models (no dependencies)
│   └── Repositories/                 # Repository interfaces
│
└── MyApp.[Service].Infrastructure/   # Infrastructure Layer
    ├── Data/
    │   ├── [Service]DbContext.cs     # EF Core DbContext
    │   ├── Repositories/             # Repository implementations
    │   └── Seeders/                  # Data seeding
    └── Services/                     # External API clients, infra services
```

**CRITICAL RULE**: Dependencies MUST flow inward:

- Domain has ZERO external dependencies
- Application depends ONLY on Domain
- Infrastructure implements interfaces from Application/Domain
- API depends on Application

### Shared Projects Location

```text
src/MyApp.Shared/
├── MyApp.Shared.Domain/              # Domain primitives, base interfaces
├── MyApp.Shared.Infrastructure/      # Logging, caching, messaging utilities
├── MyApp.Shared.CQRS/                # CQRS base classes, patterns
└── MyApp.Shared.SignalR/             # Real-time communication shared code
```

**Rule**: Only genuinely cross-cutting concerns belong in Shared projects. Service-specific logic stays in that service.
